Ranga:
  I don't know the official patch names.  The dlopen/dlclose exit()
  patch I mentioned was added to the V5.1 BL3 patch kit, thought it
  probably has another official name.  That patch kit was released
  in September 2002.  To see if you have it, type the following:

     % nm /shlib/libc.so | grep __atdlclose

  If you see no output from the above "nm" command, they you do
  not have the patch.  If you see two __atdlclose* symbols, then
  you do have the patch.  If you have the symbols, then this is
  not your problem.

  Also, make sure that the output of "ldd" on your application
  shows that it links with libpthread.so.  If it doesn't, then
  link with it.

 Joe Mario


