> We have a tru64 unix server and we're searching for a backup solution.
> We need the software and the hardware. We had a Seagate Python tape
> drive and we never got it to work properly on tru64.
> 
> What do you recommend? What do you use?
> Any advices are welcome.
> 
>   Thanks
>      Sorin

We are using a Sony AIT3 tape system and virtual disk library(large
inexpensive raid) along with Bakbones Netvault.  We backup
approximately 100-150GB nightly and about 1.5TB by weeks end.
A lot of what you "should" use is determined by what, how, how much,
TTL, etc of your data.  For a system that can be archived and
manipulated (ie: remove a portion for archive) I would go with a
tape library or similar. For incremental/consolidation backups in
which data is only held for X time I would go with a raid system
and a virtual disk library. If archiving its a bit of a toss up but
Ive had better luck keeping the price down still using tapes for
long term archivals.





