The term cluster mean "two or more servers working as one". With Tru64 both
systems share a common operating system and storage. If you system should
fail, the other system would take over the workload. Besides the common
storage, the systems have a cluster interconnect that is used for the
cluster communication between the systems. This allows the servers to talk
directly to the other systems memory for very low latency.

Each server could be running different applications, or a single application
such as an Oracle database.

Tom C
