Hi, Hns. Try to read this:
AS1200 uses 2 memory daughter cards. On each of these cards are 8 DIMM
slots. DIMMs must be installed in pairs. The maximum memory size is 4
Gbytes. Slots must be filled in order and slot 0 must contain the
largest size DIMM if different sized DIMMs are used. AS1200 employs
fixed starting addresses for DIMMs, each DIMM pair starts at a 512
Mbyte boundary. This means that if DIMMs smaller than 256 Mbyte are
used the system's
physical memory map will contain 'holes'. Supported DIMM sizes are 64
Mbytes and 256 Mbytes. The DIMMs are 72 bit SDRAM based, as the system
employs ECC.

The hole text about 5300/5305 is at: http://www.kr.freebsd.org/projects-
/i18n-flp-ko/411/texts/alpha/HARDWARE.TXT

I hope it helps.

--
Posted via http://dbforums.com


