The 5305 is an NT only version of the AlphaServer 1200. With a small
software modification (nvram instruction added) it does run VMS very well
indeed. That's why I wanted to try Tru64 as well. I mean if I'm going to run
 unix then what better than Tru64, right?
According to the hardware manual you can mix 256 and 64 MB memory, provided
that memory slot (bank) 0 has the 256 MB memory stack. That means that with
4 additional sets of 64 MB each, there are memory holes between slots 1 and
2, 2 and 3, 3 and 4, 4 and 5.
Both VMS and NT4 (yup tried that too) have no problems with that situation,
so it seemed reasonable that Tru64 would stand a chance of running too on
this, admittedly unsupported, system.

Hans



