Soon as you put :rm in you can kiss good bye local filters/effects. BSD
printing just passes all you local format requests to the remote machine to
format. Since these days most remote machines are actually HP lasers  who
also ignore the formating you loose!  What you need to do is use a bounce
queue. One queue formats the jobs and uses the input filter to lpr the
result onto a remote queue to deliver to the printer.





