Hello Folks,

  One question regarding the DCEthreads (also Posix 1003.4a Draft 4)
under Digital UNIX V4.0F: is this library an emulation layer ontop of
Posix threads?

It looks so. I have written a small program that uses DCEthreads,
compiled with cc -threads. One particularity is that it uses
pthread_sigmask, a function that only appaered in Posix 1003.1c.

The program gets compiled (it theoritically shouldn't: I would have
expected an undefined reference from ld). An odump -Dl on the binary
gives me:


                      ***LIBRARY LIST SECTION***
        Name             Time-Stamp        CheckSum   Flags Version
sig:
        libpthreads.so Apr 12 18:21:10 1999 0x4cc7972c     0 osf.1
        libpthread.so Apr 12 19:22:57 1999 0x75dd89c8     0 osf.1
        libexc.so    Apr 12 18:14:20 1999 0xbf6e7df3     0 osf.1
        libc.so      Apr 12 18:14:03 1999 0x59eef91c     0 osf.1


Thus, the Posix.1c threads library get also linked... I had a look at
/usr/include/dce/pthread.h, the definition of the API's seems to
confirm that point.

I'm almost 6 nines sure (99.9999%) that the DCEthreads library is in
reality based on the Posix.1c threads, but I'd like to get a
confirmation from an expert :-)


Thanks!
Loic.

P.S: For those who are wondering why I might actually be still
programming DCEthreads on those days, the reason is that the program
that I'm targeting is a DCE application.


